RPi::WiringPi test platform GPIO pin connections (re-derived from the test suite)

This directory was regenerated FROM SCRATCH by reading the test suite (t/*.t,
t/multi/*.pl, t/RPiTest.pm, t/crontab) as the source of truth, decoding every
device constructor against the driver submodules under ~/repos, and filling the
gaps the tests cannot prove (passive values, supply rails, the I2C level-shifter,
exact module identities) from README/FAQ/lib. See test-pinout-doc.md for the full
reference, loop-back topology, default-pin-state tables and collision analysis.

Tags: [T] proven by a test (cited)  ·  [L] submodule default the test relies on
but does not set  ·  [F] gap-filled from non-test sources.

Note: test numbers here are the CURRENT ones taken from the live suite. The OLED
tests are t/500-520 and the LCD test is t/525 (the older README referenced
t/900-909/t/920/t/925, which no longer exist).

Left of '->' is the Pi BCM GPIO (or a signal/rail); right is the destination.
Numbers in (parens) on the right are the peripheral IC's own chip pin, NOT a Pi
GPIO.

Design note: the platform is self-verifying. Every output the library drives is
looped back into an ADC (or a sister port) so a test can measure what it drove.

# I2C bus (shared: GPIO2 = SDA, GPIO3 = SCL, one pull-up pair)

    0x04  Arduino (I2C slave)     [T] t/305  (t/300 probes absent addr 0x99)
    0x20  MCP23017 expander #1    [T] t/330  (Port A<->B loopback)
    0x21  MCP23017 expander #2    [T] t/450  (stepper drive)
    0x3c  OLED SSD1306 128x64     [T] t/500-520
    0x48  ADS1115 ADC #1          [T] t/140, t/325, t/345
    0x57  AT24C32 EEPROM          [T] t/420-422   ([F] same board as RTC)
    0x68  DS3231 RTC              [L] t/320  (default addr; test sets none)
    0x77  BMP180 pressure/temp    [L] t/340  (bmp(100) arg is a pin-base)
    0x05  ATMega-328P standalone  [F] optional; not exercised by any test

# LCD (HD44780, 20x4, 4-bit; pins excluded from the pin-status check) [T] t/525

5  -> RS        4  -> D4        27 -> D6
6  -> E         17 -> D5        22 -> D7
# Note: 17 (D5) and 27 (D6) are shared with the stepper CW/CCW limit switches (t/450).

# ADS1115 ADC #1 (0x48) - analog read-back for the PWM-side devices [T]

18  -> A0   (GPIO18 PWM/servo output looped back; t/140, t/325)
            A1 <- MCP4XXXX digital-pot wiper        (t/345, reads ch 1)

# Stepper position feedback - magnetic limit switches + computed centre [T] t/450

17 <- CW limit switch     (rising-edge interrupt; t/450:118,127)
27 <- CCW limit switch    (rising-edge interrupt; t/450:122,133)
19 -> centre LED          (centre is computed from symmetric ticks, not sensed; t/450:113)

# MCP3008 ADC (SPI; CS = GPIO26, bit-banged) - SPI-side read-back [T]
#  clock/data ride hardware SPI (GPIO9/10/11) [L]; CS is bit-banged GPIO [T];
#  the hardware CE0/CE1 (GPIO8/7) are left free.

11 -> 13 (SCLK)    9 -> 12 (MISO)    10 -> 11 (MOSI)    26 -> 10 (CS)
            CH1 <- MCP4922 DAC out A                  (t/310)
            CH3 <- MCP4922 DAC out B                  (t/310)
            CH2 <- 74HC595 first Q-output (vpin 401)  (t/335)

# MCP4XXXX Digital Potentiometer (SPI; CS = GPIO13, bit-banged) [T] t/345

13 -> 1 (CS)   11 -> 2 (SCLK)   10 -> 3 (MOSI)
            wiper -> ADS1115 #1 (0x48) A1   (end terminals to 3V3/GND ref [F])

# MCP4922 DAC (SPI; CS = GPIO12, bit-banged) [T] t/310

12 -> 3 (CS)   11 -> 4 (SCLK)   10 -> 5 (MOSI)
            out A -> MCP3008 CH1     out B -> MCP3008 CH3

# 74HC595 Shift Register (fully bit-banged GPIO) [T] t/335
#  shift_register(400, 8, 21, 20, 16)

21 -> 14 (DATA/DS)   16 -> 12 (LATCH/ST_CP)   20 -> 11 (SHCP/SH_CP)
            first Q-output -> MCP3008 CH2

# Serial (UART loopback; needs the primary UART freed from Bluetooth) [T] t/315

14 -> 15 (TXD -> RXD)

# MCP23017 GPIO Expanders (two chips) - SCL/SDA on the I2C bus; RESET (chip pin 18)
#  tied high [F] (NOT Pi GPIO18).

# #2 @0x21: Bank A pins 0-3 drive the stepper via a ULN2003 [T] t/450:
A0 -> IN1   A1 -> IN2   A2 -> IN3   A3 -> IN4
# #1 @0x20: Bank A pins 4-7 loop to Bank B 4-7 for the expander GPIO test [T] t/330:
A4 -> B4   A5 -> B5   A6 -> B6   A7 -> B7    (B0-B3 unused)

# GPIO18 is multiplexed (see test-pinout-doc.md section 6) [T]

Hardware PWM/servo output (t/109, t/140, t/325), a SELF-triggered edge-interrupt
input (t/200-212; edges made by toggling the INTERNAL pull resistor, no external
driver), and a generic register/multi test pin. Its only physical connection is
ADS1115 #1 A0. Keep this net free of external pulls and loads or the interrupt
tests fail.

# Provenance / regeneration

Re-derived model:    scripts/helpers/model-from-tests.py
Regenerate visuals:  <schematic-venv>/bin/python scripts/helpers/gen-updated-visuals.py
The orchestrator injects the test-derived model into the existing renderers,
files the artifacts here, validates the KiCad project with check-kicad.py, and
diffs the re-derived model against the in-repo gen-schematic.py model. The
independent re-derivation MATCHED the in-repo model exactly. After the stepper-rig
redesign (two MCP23017s @0x20/0x21; ADS#2/0x49 removed; magnetic
limit switches on GPIO17/27 + centre LED on GPIO19), re-run the regenerators to
refresh the model and artifacts.
